        "math_academy_id": "q-66594",
        "problem": "If $tan\u2061x=\\sqrt{3},$ for some $x$, find the value of $tan\u2061(x-5\\pi ).$",
        "worked_solution": "The period of $y=tan\u2061x$ is $\\pi .$ Therefore, for integer $n$ we have\n\n$$\ntan\u2061x=tan\u2061(x+n\\pi ).\n$$\n\nSubstituting $n=-5$ into the right-hand-side of the above gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}tan\u2061x=tan\u2061(x+(-5)\\cdot \\pi )=tan\u2061(x-5\\pi ).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, if $tan\u2061x=\\sqrt{3},$ we get that $tan\u2061(x-5\\pi )=\\sqrt{3}.$",
        "actual_result": "Correct",
